Z||000002||superXmotorsports||12-10-1999||09:04 PM||||An easy 'guesstimate' is to read your MPH at 3,000RPMs and double it.  This of course assume you can overcome aerodynamic drag and have the HP to redline 5th. SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-10-1999||09:34 PM||||SuperX,<P>That is true, but what most people don't realize is that aerodynamic drag is a square function of velocity.  Therefore it truly increases exponentially.  I will try to dig up the formulas this weekend (although I am working tomorrow and leaving on a business trip Sun. a.m. so I don't know if I can get around to it).  When I find them I will try to post the pertinent ones here. <P>While I have your attn., I have heard the question asked many times about where you acquired your spoiler, but have yet to hear an answer.  Is it custom?  I guarantee that I will never try to purchase/recreate it for myself.  I don't think this mid-20's honkey (no offfense intended) can hang with that... after all I am from Ohio.  Just curious if it is custom... I am rather impressed<P>William T. Thorn, III<P>||||reg||1
